    "text": "AdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisementTRENDINGYankees shut out GiantsJudge's golden sombreroSign up for fantasy baseballOpening day starting pitchersSweet 16 previewStory byCameron Jourdan, GolfweekSun, Mar 15, 2026·3 min readAdd Yahoo Sports on GooglePONTE VEDRA BEACH, Fla. — Cameron Young is the 2026 Players champion.Young earned his second PGA Tour win in thrilling style, making birdie on the par-3 17th and then par on the 18th, including the longest tee shot in the ShotLink era on the hole, to win by one shot over Matt Fitzpatrick.AdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisementWith the win, he also earns the biggest paycheck on the PGA Tour: $4.5 million. His career earnings now sit at $31,232,516, the 58th player to surpass the $30 million mark in his career.Here's the breakdown of how much money each PGA Tour player earned from a $25 million purse at the Players Championship.Players Championship 2026 prize money payoutsPositionPlayerScoreEarnings1Cameron Young-13$4,500,0002Matt Fitzpatrick-12$2,225,0003Xander Schauffele-11$1,725,0004Robert MacIntyre-10$1,225,000T5Sudarshan Yellamaraju-9$925,000T5Jacob Bridgeman-9$925,000T5Ludvig Aberg-9$925,000T8Tommy Fleetwood-8$731,250T8Sepp Straka-8$731,250T8Justin Thomas-8$731,250T11Patrick Rodgers-7$581,250T11Brian Harman-7$581,250T13Sam Burns-6$409,027T13Akshay Bhatia-6$409,027T13Brooks Koepka-6$409,027T13Ryo Hisatsune-6$409,027T13Justin Rose-6$409,027T13Russell Henley-6$409,027T13Austin Smotherman-6$409,027T13Corey Conners-6$409,027T13Viktor Hovland-6$409,027T22Scottie Scheffler-5$271,250T22Michael Thorbjornsen-5$271,250T24J.J. Spaun-4$221,250T24Alex Smalley-4$221,250T24William Mouw-4$221,250T27Hideki Matsuyama-3$178,750T27Nicolai Hojgaard-3$178,750T27Chris Kirk-3$178,750T27Ryan Gerard-3$178,750T27Chad Ramey-3$178,750T32Eric Cole-2$128,250T32Jordan Spieth-2$128,250T32Patrick Cantlay-2$128,250T32Bud Cauley-2$128,250T32Andrew Putnam-2$128,250T32Alex Noren-2$128,250T32Max Homa-2$128,250T32Min Woo Lee-2$1